      "output": {
        "message": "Here are three practical ways to approach this while you're still relying on them for rent: 1. **Target the stable side of design.** In-house corporate design, production, or UI/UX roles often offer steady salaries and standard benefits. Showing them real job postings with clear salaries can help address their concern about stability while keeping you in the field you want. 2. **Treat a stable job as a temporary bridge.** Taking a reliable job for a set period lets you save up and take over your own rent. Once you're financially independent, you can pivot to design without needing their approval. 3. **Build your portfolio on the side.** If you have to follow their direction for the immediate future to keep your housing secure, you can use your off-hours to build a design portfolio, take freelance gigs, or build skills until you can make the leap on your own terms.",
